fw16-backlight-bpf is covered by two licences, split by directory.

1. bpf/  (the HID-BPF program and the vendored HID-BPF headers)

   GPL-2.0-only. The headers are copied from udev-hid-bpf (Copyright (c)
   2022 Benjamin Tissoires) under that licence, and the kernel requires a
   GPL-compatible licence for HID-BPF programs. Text: LICENSES/GPL-2.0-only.txt

2. Everything else  (src/, dist/, Makefile, docs/, README.md)

   MIT with the Commons Clause: free to use, copy, change and share, but not
   to sell, including paid hosting or support services whose value comes
   mainly from this software. Copyright (c) 2026 lenny1882.
   Text: LICENSES/LicenseRef-MIT-Commons-Clause.txt

Each source file carries an SPDX-License-Identifier line saying which applies.
The two parts are separate programs: the BPF object runs in the kernel, and
the service, helper script and packaging talk to it only through the kernel's
hidraw and sysfs interfaces.
